            <ArticleTitle>Churg-Strauss syndrome masquerading as an acute coronary syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313.e5-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2014.08.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(14)00536-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss Syndrome (CSS) is a rare vasculitis with multiorgan involvement. Cardiac manifestations are common causing serious complications. We report a case of CSS masquerading as a non-ST elevation myocardial infarction with heart failure. CSS should be considered in the differential diagnosis of an acute coronary syndrome(ACS)with normal coronary arteries when history of asthma, peripheral eosinophilia and multisystemic involvement is present.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
